  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technical Assistance Support to Scale Up Routine Immunisation to Internally Displaced People, Returnees and Host Communities in Hard to Reach Areas</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project contributes to increased immunization coverage of children 0 to 23 months by scaling up routine immunization services to internally displaced people (IDPs), returnees, and conflict-affected host communities residing in hard-to-reach areas in Wau, Rubkona, Abyei, and Malakal counties. Conflict, insecurity, and natural disasters have displaced nearly four million people since 2013, of whom 1.6 million are IDPs.[1] The IDPs reside in congested camps and camp-like settings, mainly in rural areas. South Sudan is also home to more than 300,000 refugees and a growing number of migrants, mainly from the region.</narrative>
  </description>
